& [HACL-001] source lock
  + [implementation] is source snapshot plus manifest
  + [proof] is passed by exact source and manifest hashes
& [HACL-002] pre-execution corpus lock
  + [implementation] is strict validator plus raw SHA-256 capture
  + [proof] is partial because the raw lock passed but frozen procedure-schema compatibility was omitted
& [HACL-003] coverage
  + [implementation] is three positive families, negatives, and form labels
  + [proof] is partial because all families and forms exist but twenty-five expected subjects are outside profile 0.1
& [HACL-004] frozen preflight
  + [implementation] is public runtime health plus expected identity comparison
  + [proof] is passed before and after execution
& [HACL-005] one route process per case
  + [implementation] is closed subprocess argument construction
  + [proof] is thirty-six of thirty-six observations
& [HACL-006] route-only boundary
  + [implementation] is mandatory --route-only argument and observation validation
  + [proof] is zero Cantor and zero llama stages with independently verified sample manifests
& [HACL-007] closed classification
  + [implementation] is one disposition enum per observation
  + [proof] is thirty-six uniquely classified observations
& [HACL-008] complete metrics
  + [implementation] is exact counts, ratios, confusion, forms, and confidence summaries
  + [proof] is passed as descriptive output with the positive-domain limitation retained
& [HACL-009] strict evidence verification
  + [implementation] is canonical UUID directory plus exact file manifest
  + [proof] is remote and copied-local verification passed
& [HACL-010] local negative tests
  + [implementation] is focused harness test suite
  + [proof] is sixteen local and sixteen EVO-X2 tests passed
& [HACL-011] noninterference
  + [implementation] is before-and-after frozen and shared identity observation
  + [proof] is runtime manifest catalogue SOP-agent hashes and llama command unchanged
& [HACL-012] honest calibration record
  + [implementation] is report, solution, proof, review, faults, narrative, attribution, and reentry
  + [proof] is passed with material successor required
